<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Golang on SpecWise Blog</title><link>https://dev-pradeep-ns.github.io/specwiseblog/tags/golang/</link><description>Recent content in Golang on SpecWise Blog</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 12 Mar 2025 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://dev-pradeep-ns.github.io/specwiseblog/tags/golang/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>blogtitle</title><link>https://dev-pradeep-ns.github.io/specwiseblog/posts/golang-setup-on-linux/</link><pubDate>Wed, 12 Mar 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dev-pradeep-ns.github.io/specwiseblog/posts/golang-setup-on-linux/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="golang-setup-on-linux">Golang Setup on Linux&lt;/h1>
&lt;h2 id="step-1-download-golang">Step 1: Download Golang&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>Download the latest Go binary from the official website:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>https://go.dev/dl/
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>For example, to download Go 1.24.1:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>wget https://go.dev/dl/go1.24.1.linux-amd64.tar.gz
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;h2 id="step-2-remove-existing-go-installation-if-any">Step 2: Remove Existing Go Installation (If Any)&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>If you have an older version of Go installed, remove it before proceeding:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>sudo rm -rf /usr/local/go
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;h2 id="step-3-extract-and-install-go">Step 3: Extract and Install Go&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>Extract the downloaded archive to &lt;code>/usr/local/&lt;/code>:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>sudo tar -C /usr/local -xzf go1.24.1.linux-amd64.tar.gz
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>&lt;strong>Note:&lt;/strong> Do not extract into an existing &lt;code>/usr/local/go&lt;/code> directory as it may cause installation issues.&lt;/p></description><content>&lt;h1 id="golang-setup-on-linux">Golang Setup on Linux&lt;/h1>
&lt;h2 id="step-1-download-golang">Step 1: Download Golang&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>Download the latest Go binary from the official website:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>https://go.dev/dl/
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>For example, to download Go 1.24.1:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>wget https://go.dev/dl/go1.24.1.linux-amd64.tar.gz
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;h2 id="step-2-remove-existing-go-installation-if-any">Step 2: Remove Existing Go Installation (If Any)&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>If you have an older version of Go installed, remove it before proceeding:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>sudo rm -rf /usr/local/go
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;h2 id="step-3-extract-and-install-go">Step 3: Extract and Install Go&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>Extract the downloaded archive to &lt;code>/usr/local/&lt;/code>:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>sudo tar -C /usr/local -xzf go1.24.1.linux-amd64.tar.gz
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>&lt;strong>Note:&lt;/strong> Do not extract into an existing &lt;code>/usr/local/go&lt;/code> directory as it may cause installation issues.&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="step-4-set-up-environment-variables">Step 4: Set Up Environment Variables&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>To use Go globally, add it to your PATH by modifying the profile file.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>For user-specific installation, update &lt;code>~/.bashrc&lt;/code>:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>echo &lt;span style="color:#e6db74">&amp;#39;export PATH=$PATH:/usr/local/go/bin&amp;#39;&lt;/span> &amp;gt;&amp;gt; ~/.bashrc
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>source ~/.bashrc
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;h2 id="step-5-verify-installation">Step 5: Verify Installation&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>Run the following command to check the installed version of Go:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>go version
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>Expected output (example):&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>go version go1.24.1 linux/amd64
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div></content></item></channel></rss>